ed above. Samples were dried in vacuum and prepared for LC-MS/MS analysis.  Sample naming information: Duplicate fragment-based drug discovery samples coded by probe (P):  Experiment 79 (P10), 82 (P11), 83 (P19), 91 (P8), 92 (P15), 93 (P13), 94 (P9), 95 (P18), 96 (P12), 100 (P14), 101 (P17), 102 (P20), 104 (P16), 105 (P6), 106 (P7), 107 (P5), 108 (P4), 109 (P2), 112 (P21), 128 (P1), 129 (P3), and 196 (P22).  The SuTex samples are untreated (K1/K5) or sotorasib-treated (K2/K6); K1 and K2 are the first bioreplicate, while K5 and K6 are the second bioreplicate; all samples analyzed twice.\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17', 'store': True, 'temperature': 0.3}}
